[agent:result]             api_key_value="DKN8DndwaAjdf98FFNSxwdVKx",
[agent:result]         )
[agent:result]         ```
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     In addition to setting function arguments directly, `hopsworks.login()` also reads the environment variables:
[agent:result]     `HOPSWORKS_HOST`, `HOPSWORKS_PORT`, `HOPSWORKS_PROJECT`, `HOPSWORKS_API_KEY`, `HOPSWORKS_HOSTNAME_VERIFICATION`, `HOPSWORKS_TRUST_STORE_PATH`, `HOPSWORKS_CERT_FOLDER` and `HOPSWORKS_ENGINE`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     The function arguments do however take precedence over the environment variables in case both are set.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Parameters:
[agent:result]         host: The hostname of the Hopsworks instance.
[agent:result]         port: The port on which the Hopsworks instance can be reached.
[agent:result]         project:
[agent:result]             Name of the project to access.
[agent:result]             If used inside a Hopsworks environment it always gets the current project.
[agent:result]             If not provided you will be prompted to enter it.
[agent:result]         api_key_value: Value of the API Key.
[agent:result]         api_key_file: Path to file wih API Key.
[agent:result]         hostname_verification: Whether to verify Hopsworks' certificate.
[agent:result]         trust_store_path: Path on the file system containing the Hopsworks certificates.
[agent:result]         cert_folder:
[agent:result]             The directory to store downloaded certificates.
[agent:result]             Defaults to the system temp directory.
[agent:result]         engine:
[agent:result]             Specifies the engine to use.
[agent:result]             The default value is `None`, which automatically selects the engine based on the environment:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             * `spark`: Used if Spark is available, such as in Hopsworks or Databricks environments.
[agent:result]             * `python`: Used in local Python environments or AWS SageMaker when Spark is not available.
[agent:result]             * `training`: Used when only feature store metadata is needed, such as for obtaining training dataset locations and label information during Hopsworks training experiments.
[agent:result]             * `spark-no-metastore`: Functions like `spark` but does not rely on the Hive metastore.
[agent:result]             * `spark-delta`: Minimizes dependencies further by avoiding both Hive metastore and HopsFS.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Returns:
[agent:result]         The Project object to perform operations on.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Raises:
[agent:result]         hopsworks.client.exceptions.RestAPIError: If the backend encounters an error when handling the request.
[agent:result]         hopsworks.client.exceptions.HopsworksSSLClientError: If SSLError is raised from underlying requests library.
